<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχλ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lewd, lustful</i>, of women
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάγνος</span> (q. v.) being used of
			men), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαχλόταται δὲ γυναῖκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					586
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ephor.
				96
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐς ἄνδρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschrio
					8.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				8.1
			</span></i>; of a man, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				11
			</span></i>; of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡδονή</span> personified,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.267
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>wanton, luxuriant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμπελος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					325
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>wanton, insolent</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					636
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
